# L §2.3 sref (sk: a literal or a place keyed by things), §5.6, §8.3 (tally 2.1.6, issue #88): lim[amt[ana]] keys
# lim by a read of the input amt, which is no place: refused LOAD-KEY, the key printed as written. tally 2.1.5's
# refcore printed its parse node's kind (LOAD-KEY index is not a key of accounts); the M0 engine prints amt[...]:
# its twin moves. T's held kplace/same-key-index.
=== base.tally
model kplace
  tally 2
  on 2026-03-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31
  note "T's base for M0's load-code fixtures (invented): a place keyed by persons, and two rows stated same at its keys; it loads clean; each fixture of codes/m0/edits.tsv changes one line"

source card "T's fixture card (invented)"

unit PLN: currency minor 0.01

kind persons

place konto[p in persons]: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..

place world: outside lives 2026-01-01..

input lim[k in accounts]: money PLN

input amt: money PLN

def twice: money PLN = amt + amt

ask q: twice

version card_2026
  cite card
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  persons + [ana] lives 2026-01-01..
  persons + [ben] lives 2026-01-01..
  amt = 1.00 PLN "the card"
  opening[konto[ana]] = 1.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "the card"
  opening[konto[ben]] = 2.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "the card"
  lim[konto[ana]] = 5.00 PLN "the card"
  lim[konto[ben]] = 5.00 PLN "the card"
  same lim[amt[ana]] = lim[konto[ben]]
=== expect
refused: LOAD-KEY amt[ana] is not a key of accounts (base.tally:37)
